  "id": "electronics.analog-circuits.transistor-switch-circuits",
  "name": "Transistor Switch Circuits",
  "level": "process",
  "parent": "electronics.analog-circuits",
  "description": "Design pedagogy for using the BJT and MOSFET as saturated ON/OFF switches (not amplifiers): cutoff and saturation regions, forced-beta base-resistor sizing, MOSFET gate drive and R_DS(on), and the canonical applications — LED driver, relay/contactor driver, light-activated switch (LDR + transistor), and dark-activated switch. The Mims 'Basic Semiconductor Circuits' entry point that bridges device physics into useful two-state control.",
